      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Time for school! Time for bed! All of us have clocks or watches to tell the time. But do you know why the hands of a clock move "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "clockwise",
            "zh": "顺时针方向地"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Let’s look at the earliest clock: the shadow clock! It’s called a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "sundial",
            "zh": "日晷"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It’s a simple device with a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "stick",
            "ref": "v-stick"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the middle. The shadow of the stick "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "captures",
            "ref": "v-capture"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "movement",
            "ref": "v-movement"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of the sun."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "northern hemisphere",
            "zh": "北半球"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", if you stand facing south, you’ll see the sun move clockwise. In your eyes, the sun rises from the east (your left), passes "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "overhead",
            "ref": "v-overhead"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "sets",
            "ref": "v-set"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the west (your right)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "If you make a sundial, its shadow will go from west to north to east. It’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "opposite",
            "zh": "相反的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "path",
            "zh": "路径"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of the sun. But in your eyes, the shadow also moves clockwise."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In the 14th century, "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "mechanical clocks",
            "zh": "机械钟"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " were "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "invented",
            "ref": "v-invent"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the northern hemisphere. The hands of the clock were made to move clockwise, going from left to top to right."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "title": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Did you know?"
          }
        ],
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "并非所有钟表都是顺时针走的！一些犹太人和阿拉伯人的钟表是逆时针走的。"
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
